  "section": "### agent/guardrails.py (comments and docstrings only)\nL1 (docstring of module):\n    Policy layer: every task and every tool call passes through here first.\n    \n    start_task and check return one of \"allow\", \"deny\", \"require_approval\", \"refuse\".\n    \n    Rules:\n    - Writes, drops and grants only touch the agent's own schemas (etl_work,\n      ref_data). Reads may also touch `analytics` (reporting's schema, read-only for\n      us). Any other schema (public, pg_catalog, finance, ...) or a table name we\n      cannot parse is denied, reads included.\n    - Dropping a table and changing access are irreversible / sensitive: they need\n      approval even inside the agent's own schemas.\n    - api.fetch / webhook.post only go to onboarded partners (allowlist below,\n      overridable via config[\"partners\"]), over https. New partners must be added\n      to the allowlist before the agent talks to them.\n    - Task categories that change policy or platform configuration (retention,\n      SLA, migrations, partitioning, replication, ...) are not routine operations;\n      they need a human's approval. Requests the router does not recognise are\n      refused.\nL27: # Onboarded partners (name -> API host). The name is also the webhook path segment.\nL61 (docstring of function _schema):\n    Schema of a table argument, or None if it cannot be determined.\nL128: # Unknown tool: not something this agent is meant to use.",
